From: John Audia <therealgraysky@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] backports: sockaddr_unsized landed in 6.18.57

Linux 6.18.57 backported struct sockaddr_unsized to include/linux/socket.h
via stable commit 946dc5835c8f ("net: Convert proto_ops bind() callbacks
to use sockaddr_unsized"), so only define it for older kernels.

Signed-off-by: John Audia <therealgraysky@proton.me>
---
--- a/backport-include/linux/socket.h
+++ b/backport-include/linux/socket.h
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 #define SOL_NFC		280
 #endif
 
-#if LINUX_VERSION_IS_LESS(6,19,0)
+#if LINUX_VERSION_IS_LESS(6,18,57)
 /**
  * struct sockaddr_unsized - Unspecified size sockaddr for callbacks
  * @sa_family: Address family (AF_UNIX, AF_INET, AF_INET6, etc.)
